Package: mateR2
Title: Simulate Single-Cohort Pedigrees Using a Constrained Bipartite Sampler
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-08-28
Authors@R: 
    person("Nicholas M.", "Sard", , "nicksard@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7695-2946"))
Description: Simulates single-cohort pedigrees for dioecious species by treating
    the mating pool as a bipartite network. A Metropolis-Hastings Markov chain
    Monte Carlo sampler, written in C++ via 'Rcpp', navigates a compressed state
    space of discrete mating-block configurations to satisfy user-specified
    targets for parental abundance, operational sex ratio and mean number of
    mates. A joint-degree-preserving edge-swapping routine then rewires the
    expanded individual-level matrix to dissolve modular block boundaries while
    holding every individual's mating success constant. Fecundity allocation,
    offspring sub-sampling, sibship and parental yield-class statistics support
    benchmarking of pedigree reconstruction software and evaluation of field
    sampling designs.
